Subject: [PATCH] qjs: a 512 KiB JS stack limit and 1 MiB of C stack on WASI

QuickJS checks its stack against a limit in linear memory (1 MiB by
default, inside upstream's 2 MiB WASI stack), but every C frame also takes
a frame on the wasm engine's own stack. The stack a suspendable (JSPI)
call runs on, which slicc-kernel's async process host uses on Cloudflare
and with createNodeKernel({ blocking: 'async' }), runs out first: deep
recursion trapped (RangeError in wasm, the process ended) instead of
throwing a catchable RangeError. With a 512 KiB default limit it throws
in both hosts; --stack-size still sets any other. The C stack keeps
upstream's 2:1 ratio to the limit at 1 MiB, which makes the initial
memory 1 MiB smaller.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@
         _WASI_EMULATED_SIGNAL
     )
     add_link_options(
-        -Wl,-z,stack-size=2097152
+        -Wl,-z,stack-size=1048576
         -lwasi-emulated-process-clocks
         -lwasi-emulated-signal
     )
--- a/qjs.c
+++ b/qjs.c
@@ -798,6 +798,10 @@
         JS_SetMemoryLimit(rt, (size_t)memory_limit);
     if (stack_size >= 0)
         JS_SetMaxStackSize(rt, (size_t)stack_size);
+#if defined(__wasi__)
+    else
+        JS_SetMaxStackSize(rt, 512 * 1024);
+#endif
     if (dump_flags != 0)
         JS_SetDumpFlags(rt, dump_flags);
     js_std_set_worker_new_context_func(JS_NewCustomContext);
